"""v16.0 — Cross-domain Deep Curriculum enrichment, pass 1.

The Otology v15.8 pass exposed a recurring problem: a topic can be present and
technically six-layered while still omitting the causal framework, decision
thresholds, operative choices, complications, variants, or the actual answer
that a Teach/Boards layer should teach.

This file performs conservative in-place enrichment of two high-consequence
canonical concepts in each of the eight non-Otology domains. It never creates
new topics and never changes concept IDs. Candidate matching is exact against a
small list of known title variants; an unmatched target is reported rather than
crashing production.
"""


def _entry(candidates, recognize, localize, workup, manage, operate, teach, tags, sources=None):
    return {
        "candidates": tuple(candidates),
        "fields": {
            "recognize": recognize,
            "localize": localize,
            "workup": workup,
            "manage": manage,
            "operate": operate,
            "teach": teach,
            "tags": list(tags),
            **({"source_basis": list(sources)} if sources else {}),
        },
    }


