            "Bilateral vocal-fold immobility usually presents as airway compromise/stridor with a surprisingly preserved voice when both folds rest near paramedian position. Do not assume bilateral recurrent-laryngeal-nerve paralysis: posterior glottic stenosis, cricoarytenoid fixation, neurologic disease, central lesions, prior intubation and post-thyroid surgery are important alternatives. The initial priority is whether the airway is safe, not whether the label is 'paralysis.'",
