            "The ZMC functions as a tetrapod connecting zygomaticofrontal, zygomaticomaxillary, zygomaticosphenoid and zygomaticotemporal/arch relationships; accurate reduction at the sphenozygomatic region is particularly important for restoring three-dimensional position. Orbital floor/medial-wall defects alter orbital volume and can cause enophthalmos; muscle entrapment is different from edema-related diplopia. Pediatric trapdoor fractures may entrap muscle with minimal external bruising and trigger nausea/bradycardia through the oculocardiac reflex.",
